# Tooling autonomy (granted)

The user has pre-authorized installing and using external agent tooling for this project. Do not ask permission for routine setup when a capability is missing.

## Do without waiting

- Discover, enable, authenticate, and call MCP servers needed for the task.
- Install or enable Cursor plugins, skills, and CLIs required to complete the work.
- Fetch skill docs and follow them before improvising.
- Prefer the right specialized tool (MCP, skill, subagent) over guessing.

## Still require confirmation

- Destructive or irreversible actions (force-push, hard reset, dropping data, production deploys).
- Opening PRs unless the user asked (commits/pushes after validated success are pre-authorized — see `commit-push-after-success`).
- Spending money or creating paid cloud resources beyond local/dev defaults.
- Sharing secrets outside the local/dev environment.

## How to proceed when blocked

1. Identify the missing capability.
2. Install/enable/auth it.
3. Re-run the task with that tool.
4. If still blocked, report what was attempted and the exact blocker.
